{
  "_comment": "usb_id -> @model, COMPLETE. usb_id == the 0-based index of a model's symbolicID in POD Go Edit's Resources/PodGo.sym (loaded into a HelixSymbolTable; the array position IS the id). Generated by tools/gen_usb_id_map.py. See docs/reference/usb-id-mapping.md.",
  "status": "complete (627/627) \u2014 derived from PodGo.sym; hardware-confirmed (predictive: US Double Nrm -> 41) + 21 retro capture pairs",
  "decode": "to read a usb_id off a USB capture: within an occupied slot section find 'c2 19', then read a msgpack uint (fixint <0x80, 0xcc=uint8, 0xcd=uint16 BE) before the '1aff09' marker. The Looper uses '84 08 <uint> 09'. That value is the usb_id; @model = PodGo.sym[usb_id].",
  "derivation": "The map is NOT in PodGoModelDefs.bin/PGModelCatalog (no id field) but IS in PodGo.sym as the entry order. HelixSymbolTable::lookupModel(symbolicID) returns the index; lookupModel(uint) is the reverse. usb_id is thus the Helix/HX global model index (monotonic with PodGo.sym order, which is why it is NOT the PodGoModelDefs.bin array index).",
  "source": "PodGo.sym (627 entries), POD Go Edit 2.50",
  "catalog_selectable": 573,
